WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.220
Transfer tools have a number of uses.

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:08.940
Here are the basic steps for transferring
stitches. With the single prong tool,

3
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.780
place it over the hook of the needle.

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.500
Pull the tool and the needle back,

5
00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.140
allowing the stitch
to fall behind the latch.

6
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.740
Push the tool and the needle forward.

7
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.700
The stitch should
automatically close the latch.

8
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.900
Keep pushing until the stitch slips off
the needle and transfers to the tool.

9
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.740
To replace the stitch on a needle
to create an eyelet or work a decrease,

10
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.260
place the hole of the tool over
the hook of the new needle.

11
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:44.540
Tilt the tool up and allow
the stitch to slip onto that needle.

12
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.460
When the stitch is securely in the hook of
the needle, remove the prong of the tool.

13
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:54.940
Use the same steps to use a two,
three, or multiprong tool.

14
00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.660
Place the tool over the hooks
of the needles to be transferred,

15
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:04.660
pull out the tool and the needles until
the stitches are behind the latches.

16
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:10.820
Push back to close the latch
and slip the stitches onto the tool.

17
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:16.440
Tilt the tool up and replace
the stitches as needed.

18
00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.260
Be sure to put the emptied needles

19
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:28.720
into working position and you
can continue knitting.

20
00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:49.290
In this example, I left the empty
needle in out of work position.

21
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.060
When I knit across, the yarn
traveled between the stitches.

22
00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.850
I then put the needle in work and continued

23
00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.440
knitting. But you can see that I
have an extra-large eyelet.

